From 03a4154e488a75dc452578776b74f24df086a284 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 03:31:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Frog hunt mode: running lean + left-arm clutch, fix head
 tracker pose

- frog_chase_pose.gd: SkeletonModifier3D layering a forward lean (Spine1/Chest),
  two-bone IK left-arm reach toward the player's chest, and finger spread/clench.
- frog_watcher.gd: HUNT mode (start_hunt/stop_hunt) with RUN -> REACH -> HOLD ->
  RECOVER cycle, 1.5 s cooldown after a miss, caught_player at <= 1.1 m.
- frog_head_tracker.gd: bone pose is parent^-1 * global in Godot 4, not relative
  to rest; the old formula aimed the head ~40-50 deg too high.
- frog_test.tscn: H toggles hunt mode, HUD shows clutch/lean/reach/grip.
- tests: hunt cycle tests plus checks on the rendered bones (BoneAttachment3D).
