From dc7f8004000c6f08f845a20798bbe57d20f73f2b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 05:06:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Frog threat timer, choke-and-lift catch, restart at the
 bedroom door

- frog_watcher.gd: threat timer (threat_enabled). Fills while the player is
  within 4 m AND looking at the frog, drains otherwise; stages at 0/2/4 s
  (snap to face, stop backing off, about to go) and hunts at 5 s.
  hold_throat()/release_throat() steer the clenched hand during a choke; the
  frog no longer turns once it has caught the player (it chased its own tail).
- frog_choke.gd: catch cinematic. Hand to the throat (0-0.4 s), lift ~0.4 m
  (0.4-1.4 s), hold with shake while the vignette closes, black at 3.4 s.
  Low side camera on the clutching-arm side, above grass height.
- player_struggle_pose.gd: hands claw at the frog's wrist (two-bone IK), legs
  kick then go limp, head forced back.
- player.gd: held flag (no input, no gravity) for cinematics.
- frog_chapter.gd: threat on for the walk back after the note; breathing from
  the frog + screen pulse at stage 3; catch -> choke -> 1.5 s black -> restart
  outside the bedroom door with the frog reset; Esc blocked during the choke.
- frog_test.tscn: J toggles the threat timer; a catch now plays the choke.
- audio: breath.wav / heartbeat.wav are generated placeholders.
- tests: threat stages, range/look/drain rules, choke on rendered bones, and
  the full stare -> hunt -> choke -> restart flow in the chapter.
